 mask and another that was  made to go with the hood with cuts and  seams that met up flawlessly beneath  each mask there was also a skull cap  mask it made breathing tough but  protected those pretty faces from  getting scratched up by the tougher  outer mask each spidey face also  featured frames around the eyes so they  could be snapped right into place and  that's why tom was able to sip through  straws  number eleven is it black and gold or  red and blue technically this suit is  kinda both since it was made to look  like the regular spidey suit but inside  out included in this eye-catching  costume were fine gold wire detailing  that would be the hidden circuitry  inside fortunately the suit wasn't so  uncomfortable as it would have been had  it actually just been the regular suit  inside out we didn't see the same suit  the team was seeing on set though the  vfx department added their own touches  to really make this suit stand out on  screen  number 12 no face or touch recognition  no access the lycra spidey suit is  useful for peter parker's high flying  his texting abilities not so much when  they're in the suits all the spider-man  actors were limited in how much they  could actually use their phones and  let's be honest with a suit that tight  it's not like there were many places  they could safely tuck their phones away  for filming anyhow number 13. it's  hybrid suit time tom was sporting a red  and black suit on set that looks very  much like what we see on screen but the  reality is what we usually see is a  fully digital suit over top of the  actor's body this digital detailing  includes layers on layers of digital  fabric including metallic inlays and  overlays all woven in together and  mimicking the movement fabric would  actually have on his body the task of  replacing the suit in all those frames  was probably most tough on the editing  team who spent hours making the  appropriately dubbed hybrid spider-man  suit a reality  number 14. the people want what they  want was anyone really a fan of the old  green goblin mask willem dafoe had heard  what was up explaining i am aware that  there was some criticism of the mask in  the original one we heard that it was  probably a consideration to change it up  a little bit they ditched the clunky old  style in exchange for a costume that's  gone above and beyond for fans even  including the classic purple hood and  for defoe the whole switch was a great  improvement as well not including the  mask meant he could hear and see  properly so you can bet the actor was a  fan of these changes  number 15 no suit left behind while the  og suits didn't all get used each of  them was on set to be used as a  reference and to recognize just how much  history was actually coming together in  this showstopper of a film the old  spidey suits were either covered in dirt  and holes or literally disintegrating  not so fun to look at or wear but they  still contain something very special all  that spidey sense love him or hate him  these suits are totally worth wearing in  the end considering just how good they  look on screen  whose spidey suit do you think had a  little extra butt padding

